  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Bauernstoss. Type: Point-Trick. Rules: Jacks > Hearts > others. Must follow suit AND Must trump. 120 points total. Partners sit opposite.',
    Player: "You hold the Old One (Jack of Clubs) and the Ace of Hearts. Your partner leads a King of trumps. Do you play the Old One to secure it, or save it? Wait, the Old One guarantees the trick. Maybe play the Ace to 'smear' 11 points?",
    objective: 'Score more than 60 points (out of 120) to win the deal.',
    gameplay: "1. **Knocking**: Before the first card is played, players can 'Knock' (Klopfen) to double the value of the game. 2. **Play**: Forehand leads. Players must follow suit (Farbzwang). If they cannot follow suit, they must play a trump (Stechzwang). If they have no trumps, they can play any card. 3. **The Trick**: Highest trump wins. If no trump, highest card of led suit wins. 4. **Scoring**: Winner of the trick takes the cards. Points are counted at the end.",
    keyRules: [
      'Jacks belong to the trump suit, not their printed suit.',
      'Stechzwang (Must Trump) applies: unlike Bavarian Schafkopf where you can discard on a void, here you MUST trump if able.',
      'Partners must cooperate without verbal signals.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: true,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '4 players in two fixed partnerships (partners sit opposite).',
      deck: '32-card German or French deck. Ranks: A, 10, K, Q(Ober), J(Unter), 9, 8, 7.',
      equipment: 'Skat pack, chalk/slate for scoring.',
      dealing: 'Deal 8 cards to each player (usually 4-4).',
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **Knocking**: Before the first card is played, players can 'Knock' (Klopfen) to double the value of the game. 2. **Play**: Forehand leads. Players must follow suit (Farbzwang). If they cannot follow suit, they must play a trump (Stechzwang). If they have no trumps, they can play any card. 3. **The Trick**: Highest trump wins. If no trump, highest card of led suit wins. 4. **Scoring**: Winner of the trick takes the cards. Points are counted at the end.",
    moveValidityConditions: {
      ante: 'Bauernstoss is a point-trick partnership game where stakes are doubled via knocking rather than using antes.',
      deal: 'The system automated dealer handles the distribution of eight cards to each of the four players at the start.',
      reveal_market: 'All 32 cards are dealt to the participants; there is no shared market or community card pool in the game.',
      buy_market: 'There is no card market in Bauernstoss; players must compete using only the eight cards they were originally dealt.',
      buy_stock: 'The entire deck is distributed during the deal phase; no cards remain in stock to be drawn or purchased.',
      fold: 'Partnerships are committed to playing out all eight tricks of the deal to determine the point winner.',
      check: 'The game uses a trick-taking structure rather than a vying structure where checks would be a valid option.',
      call: 'There is no bet to match in this game; competition is based on trick-taking efficiency and point capture.',
      bet: 'Success is measured by points earned in captured tricks rather than through financial or chip-based betting.',
      raise: 'Game stakes are doubled via the knocking mechanic rather than through escalating wagering rounds.',
      declare: 'Results are calculated automatically based on the cards in the trick pile; no separate declaration is needed.',
      reveal_hand: 'Hands stay private until cards are played into tricks; there is no dedicated reveal phase in the round.',
      award_pot: 'Winner is determined by total points on a scorecard rather than by awarding a physical or virtual pot.',
      play_card: 'Must follow suit; must trump if void in suit (Stechzwang).',
      draw: 'Every card is dealt at the start of the round; no drawing phase exists during the play of the hand.',
      discard: 'Every card in the player hand must be played into a trick; no cards are discarded or buried in this game.',
      pass: 'Allowed when rules permit skipping a wager or play.',
      bid: 'The knocking action serves as the only form of bidding to double the value of the current deal.',
      meld: 'Bauernstoss is strictly a point-trick game and does not involve the formation of sets or melds.',
      go_out: 'The deal ends automatically once all eight tricks have been played by all participants at the table.',
